	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12683"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=745" title="View the profile of Needaa">Needaa</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 41<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=miladymouse"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=miladymouse&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="miladymouse" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=miladymouse&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="miladymouse" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=745"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12683#msg12683"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12683#msg12683">Re: Sibling Punishment. . .?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #9 on:</b> November 16, 2004, 06:08:16 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							*sigh* Sibling animosity?&nbsp; 27 years ago, I, being the oldest at age 20, was left in charge of my three sisters who were then ages 15, 14 and 10, while my mother had the ominous task of arranging my father&#039;s funeral.&nbsp; Sure, we had offers from our extended family at the time, but mom, who in her entire life up till that point never left us with a babysitter decided it was better to leave the kids with me so that we&#039;d be as comfortable as we could be during that time.&nbsp; Who better?&nbsp; I knew my sister&#039;s likes and dislikes, the house rules, their bedtimes, their fears and above all my sisters knew that I would do my very best to keep them safe.&nbsp; Our time together brought us closer than anyone could ever believe.&nbsp; BUT it was the way it was presented to my sisters that helped the situation tremendously.&nbsp; Mom made everyone in charge of watching everyone else.&nbsp; Therefore, even though I was in charge my 15 year old sister &quot;watched&quot; me and my 14 year old sister &quot;watched&quot; my 10 year old sister and vice versa. It was also understood that if anyone got out of hand, we would all form a group and decide whether any one of us should get a 10-minute time out with an apology issued to the victim if necessary.&nbsp; It worked out so well that when mom started work to support our family this system kept us going without the need for babysitters who knew nothing about us and saved us major bucks when things were financially tight enough.<br /><br />I have since &quot;employed&quot; this system with my own children ages 20, 17, 13 and 9 and since I am also a stay at home mom, this doesn&#039;t happen too often, but when it does, I don&#039;t have to worry about finding a stranger to watch my kids.&nbsp; <br /><br />Sibling rivalry occurs in every family, no matter how good the parents.&nbsp; It&#039;s the way your parents handle the situation that determines whether it will continue or just become one of those &quot;passing phases&quot;.&nbsp; <br /><br />In this day and age when you can&#039;t trust strangers, even ones who have been thoroughly screened, to watch your kids, having them &quot;watch themselves&quot; at anpropriate age is still the best way to go.&nbsp; <br /><br />If you feel uncomfortable about watching your siblings then express your feelings to your parents.&nbsp; Have a family meeting where everyone can &quot;air&quot; their thoughts/objections, etc.&nbsp; Just know that when your parents put you in this situation they have developed trust in you and that is the &quot;ultimate&quot; in compliments... you have shown them through your actions that you are responsible enough to be in charge and not have to have someone watch over you. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Needaa Spiritfyter<br />Guild Leader, Dark Empire
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
